{
  "_": "Who each model is: its character and tier. The tiers are four, weakest to strongest: chibi, middle, high, university. A model in `lineup` is that exact pick, and the lineup is the roster's mainstream models, shown even before you can use them; `models` names who other models are, by id or pattern (`*` any run of characters, `?` one character; first match wins), with no card of their own until a provider offers them; any other model is matched by `match` (its id, without any 'vendor/' prefix) or by its provider, and its tier by the words in its id (`words`, first hit wins; else `fallback`). `ignored` (ids or patterns) are last generation's models the roster leaves out until you choose them: a provider that serves its whole catalog shows them as Ignored under Models & keys. `home` is the provider the roster offers a character's models from when DSH does not offer them yet (through OpenRouter as `vendor`/model). How each character looks and what she and the tiers are called is the art pack's (art/pack.json); your own picks in the roster win over both.",
  "characters": {
    "gpt": { "home": "openai", "match": ["^gpt", "^o\\d", "^chatgpt", "^codex", "^openai"], "providers": ["openai", "openai-codex", "azure"] },
